eally unattractive so in  order that Putin has good options here  some that he wants to pursue he's faced  with a bunch of lousy options and he has  to choose the least bad of those  um and that's why I think it's strongly  in our interests to make that negotiated  ceasefire the least bad of these  different options that Putin has to  choose right now you know Putin is a  position that many leaders find  themselves when they launch Wars that  prove a lot less successful than they  hoped they would be and at the end of  the day almost all wars end through a  negotiated process in which each side  has to make agonizing concessions that  it hates to make  my point is that we should try to speed  up that process  um so that you know we we make Putin as  likely as we can do there's a lot here  that's out of our control we want to  make it as likely as possible that Putin  takes this place saving way out of this  crisis as soon as possible uh in a way  that doesn't involve like the  destruction of Ukrainian cities or Worse  still the use of nuclear weapons  um so that would be the the kind of  positive trajectory  um where the West can try to nudge uh  Putin towards a a positive or A least  bad outcome  um what's the alternative where do you  see the risk of a chain of escalations  that lead to a nuclear use  there's various Pathways that you can  imagine but the one that honestly  worries me the most in this situation is  the pathway in which Putin's nuclear  threat on this occasion fail as I think  they will like I don't think they're  going to cause  Ukraine to back down or the US and its  allies to back down and Putin is left  fighting a bloodbath of a prolonged  conventional War  um in which the Russian economy is in  tatters Russian soldiers are being  killed left right and Center there is no  end in sight of this conflict in which  Putin perhaps starts to worry about  whether his his rule at home might be  threat like I don't know whether that's  likely or not but 