ar weapons to be used  conversely you know Russia also has a  large variety of non-strategic Delivery  Systems that can't reach the United  States on a day-to-day basis those  Delivery Systems are not stored with  nuclear warheads if we saw Russia start  to move nuclear warheads from the  storage locations to the deployment  location of its non-strategic weapons  then Russia would likely be trying to  convey Earth nuclear threat to the  Ukraine and in that case if it ended up  in nuclear use then I think the target  would be Ukraine so I I think we will  know a bit more about possible scenarios  uh when and if Russia's nuclear positive  visibly changes in the next few days  like hopefully it won't but if it does  that will give us a bit more about I  think uh tell us a bit more about  Putin's thinking  um and where is the the deterrent effect  of the West's nuclear forces here  um because we're we're talking about  actions which would see Vladimir Putin  using nuclear weapons where nobody else  has used them and facing the potential  for a some kind of massive retaliation  perhaps also in a nuclear sense so  why is it why why these thoughts even  possible given the potential uh  retaliatory consequences well I mean  firstly Richard I point out that this  kind of nuclear use is not unprecedented  in fact it's the only precedented form  of nuclear use is nuclear used to try to  end a conventional War  um in a way to avoid a huge amount of  conventional fighting obviously the big  difference between the end of the second  world war in the Pacific and today is  Japan didn't have a nuclear armed Ally  in 1945 Ukraine the us is not a formal  Ally but it's a friend of Ukraine and I  you know I think the U.S nuclear forces  and French and British nuclear forces  will work heavily on Putin's psychic he  will be fully aware that the use of  nuclear weapons could lead to  retaliation that's why I think he's  unlikely to do it  um but I think the the rationale here is  that he 